  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#37298\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before in PowerToys#37298. The File Explorer preview pane doesn't update an already-loaded SVG when you switch Windows between dark and light mode. The ticket is filed as a feature request to apply theme changes directly in the preview pane, and it doesn't describe a fix or a setting that keeps the preview in light mode. To work around it, hide and re-show the preview pane, select the file again, or reopen the Explorer window after switching themes. The SVG will then re-render with the current theme. For the wider question of SVG background colour, such as white-on-white visibility, see PowerToys#2516, which discusses checkered or custom background options.\"}",
